PATCH_ID: 003
TYPE: feature_architecture

INTENT:
Extend emulator system to support three-generation handheld runtime (GB, GBC, GBA) under a unified mode router with auto-detection, while preserving JARVIS GitHub cyberspace + grid shell architecture.

CONTEXT:
System currently supports GB core + GitHub-based JARVIS runtime. This patch introduces:
- GBC compatibility via GB core extension
- GBA support via separate emulator core (WASM/JS)
- unified ROM loader + auto detection
- grid OS integration for mode selection
- strict runtime isolation between cores and JARVIS system

SCOPE:
- EmulatorRouter (core selection system)
- ROMLoader (auto-detect GB/GBC/GBA)
- GBCore (existing compatibility baseline)
- GBACore (new WASM/JS wrapper abstraction)
- ModeController update (3-gen support)
- Grid OS node integration for ROM selection
- unified emulator interface contract

CHANGES:

- Define unified EmulatorCore interface:
  - loadROM(buffer)
  - start()
  - stop()
  - update(dt)
  - optional save/load state

- Implement EmulatorRouter:
  - manages active core instance
  - switches between gb_core / gba_core
  - ensures only one active runtime at a time
  - isolates execution contexts per mode

- Add GBACore wrapper:
  - integrates WASM or JS-based GBA emulator engine
  - exposes unified EmulatorCore interface
  - runs independently of GB/GBC core

- Extend GB core usage:
  - GB and GBC handled by same core module (compatibility mode)

- Add ROMLoader:
  - detects ROM type (gb / gba)
  - routes to correct emulator core
  - supports user file input (ArrayBuffer)
  - no GitHub ROM hosting dependency

- Update ModeController:
  - supported modes:
    - "grid_home"
    - "gb_rom"
    - "gba_rom"
    - "jarvis_ui"
  - transitions automatically based on ROM detection

- Grid OS integration:
  - add ROM selection node:
    - GB selection
    - GBA selection
    - “Import ROM” entry point
  - grid only routes, does not execute

- Define strict isolation rules:
  - GB/GBA cores cannot access GitHub FS
  - JARVIS runtime cannot access emulator memory
  - Grid shell is navigation-only layer
  - ROM execution is local-device only

- Add unified boot flow:
  - GRID loads first
  - user imports ROM or selects node
  - ROMLoader detects type
  - EmulatorRouter activates correct core
  - execution begins in isolated runtime

CONSTRAINTS:
- no implementation of full emulator engines required in this patch
- GBA core defined as wrapper abstraction only
- no ROM hosting on GitHub
- no backend or server dependencies
- must remain browser-compatible (GitHub Pages)
- maintain strict separation between:
  - execution layer (emulators)
  - UI layer (grid + JARVIS)
  - data layer (GitHub repo assets)

OUTPUT EXPECTATION:
- system supports:
  - Game Boy + Game Boy Color execution (shared core)
  - Game Boy Advance execution (separate core abstraction)
  - unified ROM loading + auto detection
  - grid-based navigation entry point
  - JARVIS GitHub cyberspace runtime remains intact
